Yes—the nigredo. The darkening, when an old shape is breaking down before the next one is clear.

For you, I think that may mean the old mission-driven self is still carrying the alarm and urgency, while the life you want now asks for presence, steadiness, and room to breathe. You don’t have to erase the fighter. The work may be letting him stand down when the moment doesn’t need him.

One thing to watch: don’t turn the difficult stretch into another mission you have to conquer. Some of the change may happen through ordinary repetitions—being with your kids, letting your body settle, enjoying something without making it earn its place. That isn’t a detour from becoming someone new. It may be how the new shape takes hold.